          "text": "On admission, blood glucose was 'HI' on BM (laboratory glucose 34), ketones 5.2, pH 7.18, and bicarbonate 11, consistent with severe DKA. She was managed on the ward HDU with PICU informed. The DKA protocol was commenced with cautious IV fluids, fixed-rate insulin infusion, potassium replacement, and hourly monitoring. By Day 2, pH had improved to 7.34 and ketones to 0.8. She was transitioned to subcutaneous insulin on a basal-bolus regimen. The paediatric diabetes nurse and dietician provided input, and structured family education — including carbohydrate counting, hypo management, and sick-day rules — was initiated. (Specialty: Paediatrics (Diabetes) — inferred — not documented, confirm)",
